IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2867 of 2012
CITATION: (2009) 9 SCC 221
YEAR: 2009

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: S.B. Sinha, Deepak Verma

PARTIES:
Malay Kumar Ganguly vs Dr. Sukumar Mukherjee

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 1986, Indian Penal Code, 1860

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 304A IPC, Section 14 Consumer Protection

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
standard of medical care, gross negligence, record compensation, toxic epidermal necrolysis

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Awarded unprecedented medical negligence damages, ruling that hospitals and consulting doctors are strictly liable for deviations from standard clinical treatment protocols.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 304A IPC, Section 14 Consumer Protection.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

